  "id": "es-acentos",
  "title": "¿Dónde está el acento?",
  "language": "es",
  "feedback_mode": "immediate",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "explanation",
      "markdown": "Every Spanish word has one stressed syllable. A written accent (*tilde*) marks it when the usual rules would put the stress elsewhere: *can-**ción***, *te-**lé**-fo-no*. Without a tilde, words ending in a vowel, *n* or *s* stress the second-to-last syllable: *ca-**mi**-no*."
    },
